    "Classify the sentiment of the following text as Positive or Negative.",
    "Classify the sentiment of the text as Positive or Negative. \n\nWhen encountering conflicting evidence, follow these rules:\n1. Primary Intent: Prioritize the overall emotional valence and primary intent over secondary qualifying adjectives or critical caveats. If the core sentiment is praise despite nuanced critiques, classify as Positive.\n2. Logical Resolution: Carefully resolve double negatives, comparative mitigations, and linguistic inversions. Ensure that phrases describing a relative improvement or the absence of a negative quality are not misclassified as Negative.\n\nReturn only \"Positive\" or \"Negative\".",
    "Classify the sentiment of the following text as either Positive or Negative. \n\nTo ensure accuracy:\n1. Determine the primary emotional valence. If a text contains both praise and criticism, prioritize the overall intent and main sentiment over secondary qualifying adjectives or minor caveats.\n2. Carefully resolve logical inversions, double negatives, and comparative mitigations. Ensure that negative markers used to describe a relative improvement or a lack of failure are processed as positive or neutral rather than negative.\n\nReturn only the label: Positive or Negative.",
