  "diagnosis": "The errors fall into two distinct semantic failure patterns:\n\n**1. Nuanced Positive/Mixed Sentiment (False Negatives)**\nThe model fails to recognize \"qualified\" praise. When positive sentiment is coupled with critical caveats (e.g., conceptual interest vs. execution) or complex emotional descriptors (e.g., affection mixed with pity), the model over-indexes on the critical terminology and misclassifies the overall intent as negative.\n*   **Rule:** Prioritize the primary emotional valence over secondary qualifying adjectives.\n\n**2. Double Negatives/Comparative Mitigation (False Positives)**\nThe model struggles with linguistic mitigation. It identifies negative markers (e.g., \"worse\") but fails to process the logical inversion created by the preceding negation. This results in the model detecting \"badness\" without understanding that the phrase actually describes a relative improvement or a lack of total failure.\n*   **Rule:** Resolve logical inversions and comparative qualifiers before assigning a final sentiment polarity.",
